# These are error-branch variants in the no-follow append/read paths. The
# create/open branches are selected only by kernel errno races; each fallback
# still retries with O_NOFOLLOW or returns an empty/failed closed result. The
# <= loop boundary only permits one zero-byte read after the capped buffer is
# full, which has the same result as <.
crates/frank-safeio/src/unix.rs:122:19: replace match guard e == rustix::io::Errno::NOENT with true in open_append_create
